Posters for my four most recently watched movies, as logged on Letterboxd (right to left):
House (2½ out of 5 stars)— way too much going on here;
Gremlins 2: The New Batch (4½ out of 5 stars)— delightful non-stop mayhem in this all-timer;
Roar (1981) (unrated) (liked)— look, I really like cats too, but letting them maul your family for 11 years for your vanity film project is a bit much;
and You Can See Everything (4½ out of 5 stars)— If everything is a performance, what does the truth even mean?

